Redrob OS
=========

This machine runs Redrob OS, a bootable-container (bootc) image built from
https://github.com/redrob-labs/redrob-os and published as
ghcr.io/redrob-labs/redrob-os. The whole operating system is one signed image;
`bootc status` shows which one is booted and which one is staged.

Where things are
----------------
  /usr/share/redrob/pins-installed.env   versions of the binaries baked into this image
  /usr/bin/redrob-launcher               Redrob Launcher (installs/updates the Redrob apps)
  /usr/libexec/gvisor/                   gVisor runsc, the agent task sandbox runtime
  /etc/containers/policy.json            requires a signature on every Redrob OS image
  /etc/greenboot/check/                  boot health checks (red boot -> automatic rollback)
  /var/lib/redrob/                       machine state (first-boot markers, device id)

Updates
-------
  System : bootc-fetch-apply-updates.timer, daily ~03:00, staged, applied at next reboot.
           Manual: `sudo bootc upgrade` then reboot. Roll back: `sudo bootc rollback`.
  Apps   : Flathub via Discover; redrob-flatpak-update.timer (per user, daily).
  Redrob : Redrob Launcher keeps Redrob Browser/Office/Canvas/Code current in your home.

Developer notes live in the repository under docs/image.md.

